WEBVTT

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:33.380
Ishimura (Ishi)
Graveposts

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.070
Wow!

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.290
So cool!

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.780
Thanks for always splitting
them so precisely.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.640
You're a big help, Nonoha.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.080
So strong! She's like a monster!

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.260
Miss Monster, this time
break a bigger one!

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.790
I... I'm not some sideshow, you know.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.330
And would you stop calling
me "Miss Monster"?

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.180
That really is amazing.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.020
You've always been
good at sports, haven't you, Nonoha?

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.030
Nonoha's breaking has
gotten more powerful.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.140
More to the point, what's up
with this surreal situation?

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.280
The truth is, last week...

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:56.000
She saved a kid who was
gonna get hit by a truck.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.500
Since then, they've taken
to her in a weird way.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.870
Like what you see.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.730
Okay, students of Root
Gakuen's kindergarten,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.080
do what Miss Madoka tells you,

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.990
and have fun and study, okay?

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.630
Okay!

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.330
See you next time, Madoka.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.870
I'm glad Madoka is doing well.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.860
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.590
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:01.440
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.180
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:08.690
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:13.400
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.620
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.270
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.280
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.580
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.520
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.340
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:31.840
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.140
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.830
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:41.050
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.390
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:46.020
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:51.910
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.590
Brain diver

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.390
Brain diver

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:10.960
Nonoha's Title

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:21.440
Why must one such as I
remain on the first floor?

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.090
And eat plain noodles I pay for myself?!

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.450
That's right.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.930
You even beat Daimon in that challenge.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.410
It can't be helped.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:32.620
Titles can't be traded between students.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.060
The principal said so.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.180
By rights, it should be ME up there!

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.110
On Genius Terrace, living the good life!

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.660
Puzzle rings are difficult, huh?

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.250
I think I might not be good at puzzles...

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:53.260
I, Ana, think that is
definitely a love letter!

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:56.000
Judging from the
circumstances, it must be!

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.110
Meaning that Kaito's charm comes

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:01.140
shining through, even for the layperson.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.610
I don't believe it.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:05.580
That lady teacher
has a thing for lowlifes.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:06.980
Come on, everyone.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.370
Don't assume it's a love letter.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:12.440
Madoka wouldn't be interested in
a lunkhead like this guy.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.100
Who're you callin' a lunkhead?

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:18.230
I... I am absolutely,
positively not interested!

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.760
I just wonder, why won't you

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.050
show me the letter, Kaito?

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:24.070
It's got nothin' to do with ya.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:25.890
What's with that attitude?!

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.270
My puzzle ring!

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.250
Ah, shut up. I don't wanna talk to some

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.990
sweets of mass destruction-makin' chick like you!

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.630
I, Ana, think they're super good.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.970
I'd say they're practically genius-level.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.740
Oh, run for it, Kaito!

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:44.800
SO sorry for the "sweets
of mass destruction"!

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:46.840
I give up! I give up! I give up!

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.650
Nonoha fairly SHINES today as well!

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:52.140
She's got those "geniuses"
around her little finger.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.990
That Daimon is insufferable,
but she seems to

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:57.350
have plenty of problems of her own...

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.070
Fall!

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:06.530
Upperclassman Itou!

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:07.870
So cool!

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.710
Nice shot, Nonoha!

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.840
Miss Itou is TOO cool!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.890
She's great at sports, makes straight As,

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.670
and is so pretty! Aah, I adore her!

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.600
And that memory of hers.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.380
She's, like, genius!

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:35.560
<i>Being all wishy-washy isn't like me.</i>

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.270
<i>
I need to make things clear.</i>

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:42.190
POG Japan has had a change in personnel.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.310
It seems the general director has been dismissed.

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:46.840
Huh?

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:48.990
Apparently, the general
director's actions

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:52.160
were not understood by his superiors.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.660
You don't get it, do you?

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:56.800
Why should the head office
pardon such liberties?

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.590
Baron and you, men of doubtful origin

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.500
who appear to have popped out of nowhere...

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:06.050
What is required for
Philosopher's Puzzles?

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.970
It is FEAR.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:13.680
The beautiful fear and death
that awaits those who desire the prize.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.180
THAT is a Philosopher's Puzzle.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:20.610
Use the Philosopher's Puzzle
to eliminate a maggot.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:23.500
That is the order from head office, yes?

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.320
That is incorrect.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.190
As with head office, Mr. Rook intends-

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.230
I have no objection to your thinking.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.070
Mr. Rook...

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:35.450
I have already taken steps.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.290
Come back once you've witnessed

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:40.360
the beautiful machinations
of Herbert Mueller,

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.420
Chief of POG Far East Headquarters.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.040
I look forward to it.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:52.970
No. I ain't showin' you the letter.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.640
But why? Why not?!

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.230
You like that Madoka person, right?

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:01.630
Yes. She lives in the neighborhood,

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.650
and she's looked out for me for years.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:06.540
She's kind and loves kids,

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.920
and was able to
become a kindergarten teacher.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:11.930
I was worried about her after
her fiancé died, but...

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:13.530
Fiancé?

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:15.900
Last year. He got sick.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:19.240
I'm sure it was hard on Madoka. But...

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.970
<i>It's all right, Nonoha.</i>

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:29.530
<i>I've decided I'm going
to continue his dream.</i>

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:30.910
<i>Masaru's dream.</i>

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.390
She's a good person, Madoka.

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:36.940
Continue his dream?

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.890
So her fiancé was...!

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:50.650
Beat it!

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:54.200
Our apologies!

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.240
Gammon.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:57.700
Yo, Nonoha.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:00.780
Some guys were talkin' bad about ya,

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.200
but I put 'em in their place!

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:03.000
About ME?

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.660
That you're bad at puzzles.

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.170
That you don't have a title,

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.360
but you act all big up on Genius Terrace.

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:13.500
So I told 'em. Nonoha DOES have a title:

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.720
"Miss Monster," a splendid title indeed!

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.430
I don't need some stupid title!

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:21.630
If I got one, I'd be branded a weirdo,

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:24.920
my life would fall apart! I'd be sub-human, game over!

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:27.740
Huh? Where's Kaito?

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:31.900
Oh, darn it!

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:32.850
What gives?

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:35.430
He's gonna go meet Madoka!

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:37.790
That letter would say a time or a place...

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:38.900
We're going after him!

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.230
Me, too?

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:42.640
Now look, I don't really-

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:43.660
Just come on!

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:53.280
<i>Hey, Kaito, wait!</i>

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:56.460
<i>There's no way YOU'RE
gonna catch me, Nonoha!</i>

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:09.680
Sure enough, their meeting place was
Root Kindergarten, huh?

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:11.790
I'm in good form today.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:15.740
Why are you so concerned about Kaito?

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.700
Huh? Beats me. Why is that?

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.280
Don't ask me...

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:32.800
It's time. Come out!

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:36.550
You put your shoes on?

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.180
Ah, it's Monster's boyfriend!

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.150
Monster's boyfriend! Monster's boyfriend!

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:43.590
What do you think you're doing?

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:46.090
They're going to help me, the Giver!

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:48.060
You'd use innocent children?!

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:50.510
That's the order from the top.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:51.520
What?!

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:56.450
It's all right. They're good kids,
and they learned the plan quickly.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.850
Ah! It's Miss Monster!

00:09:58.850 --> 00:09:59.930
Miss Monster!

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:02.350
Break a big rock!

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:02.830
Yes, Nonoha came, too...

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:04.570
Who's next to her?!

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:04.730
This is a surprise!

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:08.830
A teacher at Root's
Kindergarten is a Giver for the POG, eh?

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.340
I took on his dream.

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:15.090
To become the greatest Giver;
that was Masaru's dream.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:18.710
Nonoha... I didn't want you to know this!

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:33.640
Wh..What is this place?

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:35.110
Yeesh, scary!

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:37.570
It's the old nursing
academy, now in ruins.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:40.490
I get it.

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.600
So that would explain Nightingale, huh?

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:48.870
The puzzle that Masaru made awaits.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.040
Teacher, I'm scared...

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.030
I wanna go home!

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.460
It's all right. If you
do like we practiced,

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.760
you can go home soon.

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:03.680
What is it? You won't
listen to your teacher?

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.750
Don't make this difficult for me.

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:06.990
What are you saying?

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.490
If you bring them to a place like this,

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:11.560
of course they're going to be scared!

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.570
Do you not even understand THAT anymore?

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:18.400
Where did she go, the Madoka
that cared for children?!

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:26.490
Let's go, everyone. Come with me.

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:32.640
Aw, crap! We're locked in!

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:35.070
<i>There is no going back.</i>

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.190
Who're you?!

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:40.810
<i>Unless you solve the
Philosopher's Puzzle,</i>

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:43.260
<i>
the door will not open.</i>

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:45.900
The lives of not just you vermin
but also the CHILDREN is at stake.

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:49.610
That's why you involved
the kids in this?!

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:53.160
<i>Accidents happen in abandoned buildings.</i>

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.800
<i>Should something occur not related to the puzzle,</i>

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.030
<i>I would ask you attribute it to bad luck.</i>

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.490
<i>After all, it wouldn't be unusual</i>

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:03.030
<i>for this building to collapse at any moment.</i>

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:08.040
Fall victim to beautiful fear...

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:11.950
May you die an unsightly
death, Kaito Daimon.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:16.750
No... I wasn't told that!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.210
You get it now, Madoka?

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:21.480
THIS is the POG.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:23.470
I don't know what the

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.630
POG was like when Masaru was alive...

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:27.540
But this is how they are now!

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:30.900
The POG would even toy with the lives of children!

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:39.390
I'm scared!

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:41.960
I wanna go home!

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:45.620
What should we do? I... I...!

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:47.970
If we don't hurry, things
will get real bad!

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:48.930
Dammit!

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:52.490
Everyone!

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.210
Let's all play together.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:00.450
It's a puzzle, okay? A puzzle.

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:02.970
If we have to do it, we may as well have fun!

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:08.180
Okay!

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:10.970
Nonoha...

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.720
Puzzle time... Let's begin!

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:18.980
Herbert Mueller...

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:21.940
The hidden face of the POG.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:23.890
A ruthless man who takes ordinary puzzles

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:27.150
and turns them into vicious ones.

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:30.690
He will be a tough one, Kaito.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:34.740
There are three puzzles total.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:37.370
This is the first room!

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:41.380
All right, let's knock this thing out!

00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:43.880
Yelp!

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:49.620
I'll break this person apart,

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:51.980
so please put him together again!

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.050
I-It's a skeleton...

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:01.500
Oh jeez, again?

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.960
Leave it to me.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:06.860
Everyone, your attention please!

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:16.870
Huh? Why?!

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.710
Ah! The puzzle's suddenly started!

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:25.260
Dammit! There are too many pieces.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.860
Hurry! Gather the bones!

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:27.880
The bones! The bones!

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:43.900
This completes it.

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:48.320
The door over there opened!

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:17.240
This is the second puzzle.

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:21.650
What's with that eye chart?

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:23.310
It's a maze.

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:25.170
You start at the arrow,

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:27.390
heading for the goal at the very bottom.

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:30.430
You can only go through
where the C-shape is broken.

00:15:30.430 --> 00:15:33.980
If it's broken in two directions,
you can choose either one.

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:36.900
Shoot! Sure I could solve it,

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.510
but it gets small and I can't see it!

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.960
I can see it, but I can't solve it.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:43.180
Pops, I gotta pee!

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:44.230
Me, too.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:45.210
And me.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:48.430
Now listen! Right now,
"Pops" is solvin' a puzzle.

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:50.630
And I ain't yer Pops.

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:04.840
Aargh! I can't concentrate!

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:05.770
Gammon!

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:07.480
Do some funny faces
and make them stop crying!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:09.030
Why do I have to?!

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:09.860
Do it.

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:11.860
Dammit!

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:18.870
No. This ain't me...

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:24.550
Okay, solved it!

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:25.960
You did it, Kaito!

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:38.220
That, huh?

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:41.620
This is the last puzzle.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:43.230
Please do your best.

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:46.230
This won't hold much longer. Let's hurry.

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:52.360
Look out!

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:02.120
Nonoha!

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.420
You okay, Nonoha?!

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:09.200
Yes. Just scratches. You okay?

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.390
Miss!

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:15.380
I'm glad you're all
right. I really am glad.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.950
Damn! What're we gonna do, Kaito?

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:33.460
The puzzle's gone!

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.450
It's okay. Nonoha remembers it.

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:37.700
You can do it, right, Nonoha?

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:38.680
Huh?

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:40.700
Yes!

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:11.730
Awesome...

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:15.990
Kaito. Gammon. Okay.

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:22.250
This is a picture-coloring puzzle, huh?

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:22.990
Yeah.

00:18:23.570 --> 00:18:26.340
The letters inside each circle are the

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:28.770
first part of the word for a color.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:34.900
"B" is blue, "G" is green,
"R" is red, "V" is violet.

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:39.010
"O" is orange, "W" is
white, "Y" is yellow.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:40.920
So that's it.

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:44.410
Everyone, let's do some coloring!

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:46.310
Okay!

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:00.620
Looks like fun, huh?

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.170
Even in this situation...

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:03.750
It's the puzzle.

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:07.290
The kids understand the
kindness of the guy who made this puzzle.

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:10.780
Miss Madoka!

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.190
You do it, too!

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:19.800
Here! You do red!

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:24.050
Thank you.

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:32.950
Madoka.

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:36.530
Taking on the dream of your
loved one isn't a bad thing.

00:19:36.970 --> 00:19:40.410
But please always be yourself.

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:41.960
For the children's sake.

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:44.530
Nonoha...

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:48.160
Okay, it's finished!

00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:50.540
And the answer is?

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:52.800
One, two...

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:55.540
Nightingale!

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:07.290
It seems this level of
fear is insufficient.

00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:18.230
A golden Nightingale bust!

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:20.630
If that's really gold, that's awesome!

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:23.200
Up till now, it's been paintings
and cars and sunsets,

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.240
crap prizes that make no sense.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.700
This is a treasure that
SEEMS like a treasure!

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:30.750
This belongs to Nonoha and those kids,
who said the answer.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:31.730
What'll you do?

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:33.750
Donate it to children in need!

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:39.400
You're so cool, Miss Nightingale!

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:40.820
So rugged!

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:42.420
You're the greatest!

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:47.440
They bumped your title up
from "Monster" to "Nightingale"

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:48.430
What a waste!

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:53.440
<i>Charity... Dedication... Nightingale...</i>

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:59.440
<i>Nonoha and the children have made me
ME again, Masaru.</i>

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:09.030
All that happened yesterday?

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:11.480
He did well and cleared the puzzle.

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:12.410
Kaito...

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:14.670
You knew, didn't you?

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:16.250
That the girl was a Giver.

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:20.900
Root Kindergarten is, after
all, part of this Gakuen.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:23.390
I have made it so she will continue

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:25.390
to work at the kindergarten.

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:28.260
Of course, she shall retire as a Giver.

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:31.840
I can understand the shock that she felt.

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:34.070
The difference between the POG

00:21:34.070 --> 00:21:36.270
she'd imagined and the current POG...

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:40.020
The Puzzle of God and
the existence of the

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:42.280
Phi-Brains has unbalanced everything.

00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:46.890
By the way, did you know?

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:50.280
The Gakuen has allowed
Nonoha to have a title.

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:51.790
What?

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:58.830
If Itou is "Nightingale,"
it's the end of the world.

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:02.250
That's one Nightingale who
ain't no "White Angel," huh?

00:22:02.930 --> 00:22:04.870
NOOOO!

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:08.360
I do NOT want a title, no!

00:22:08.360 --> 00:22:09.590
I don't want weirdoes for friends!

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:12.470
I don't want to be no good!

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:12.470
Aah, shut up. You're ruinin' my lunch.

00:22:13.860 --> 00:22:15.010
I'm done for!

00:22:15.010 --> 00:22:17.990
I can't go on to college!
I can't get a job!

00:22:17.990 --> 00:22:20.340
I can't even get married!

00:22:20.340 --> 00:22:22.260
Gammon, your cheeks are red.

00:22:23.270 --> 00:22:25.610
One hundred percent...

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:27.920
NOOOOO!

00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:41.490
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:47.410
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.410 --> 00:22:52.040
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:57.090
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:02.570
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:07.930
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:13.110
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:18.360
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:23.700
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:26.380
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:29.290
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.290 --> 00:23:33.860
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:39.160
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:44.440
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:49.980
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:49.980 --> 00:23:58.920
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.090 --> 00:24:06.120
We're here! In Hokkaido!

00:24:06.120 --> 00:24:07.980
It's so wide-o!

00:24:07.980 --> 00:24:10.370
I'm gonna eat a TON of crab!

00:24:10.370 --> 00:24:12.340
A ton of it!

00:24:12.340 --> 00:24:14.850
I'm gonna eat a TON of sorghum, too!

00:24:14.850 --> 00:24:16.700
A ton!

00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:19.390
Is there anything else you want to eat?

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:21.560
Hmm... Moss balls?

00:24:21.830 --> 00:24:25.110
Next time: "Crab! Hot
Springs! The Puzzle King!"

00:24:21.920 --> 00:24:27.720
Crab! Hot Springs! The Puzzle King!

00:24:25.110 --> 00:24:27.810
Um, moss balls are an
endangered species...
